  "type": "problem",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Two equally sized maps mark land with <code>1</code> and water with <code>0</code>. An island in <code>grid2</code> is a sub-island if every one of its cells is also land in <code>grid1</code>. Count qualifying islands; one unmatched cell disqualifies its entire connected island.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid1 = [[1,1,0],[0,1,0],[1,0,0]], grid2 = [[1,1,0],[0,1,0],[0,0,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1</pre>\n  <p>The upper-left island is fully covered; the other grid2 cell is not.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid1 = [[1,0],[0,1]], grid2 = [[1,1],[0,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>The grid2 island contains a cell over water.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid1 = [[1]], grid2 = [[1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1</pre>\n  <p>The sole island is entirely covered.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= rows, columns &lt;= 100</code>; empty matching grids have answer zero.</li>\n    <li>Both grids have identical rectangular dimensions and contain only <code>0</code> or <code>1</code>.</li>\n    <li>Connectivity uses sides, not corners.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def countSubIslands(self, grid1: List[List[int]], grid2: List[List[int]]):\n        \"\"\"NUMBER\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "class Solution {\n  /** Return the required number result. */\n  countSubIslands(grid1, grid2) {\n    // your code here\n  }\n}\n"
  },
